        "fx_desc_blur_gaussian": "Smooth, adjustable blur with a direction — you can blur a single axis.",
        "fx_desc_blur_lens": "Lens blur: a disc of samples shaped like the iris, where bright areas weigh more — this is bokeh, not a smear.",
        "fx_desc_blur_sharpen": "Brings out detail and edges without inventing texture.",
        "fx_desc_blur_unsharp": "A real unsharp mask: original + gain × (original − blurred), with a threshold so grain is not amplified.",
        "fx_desc_color_brightness_contrast": "Raises brightness and opens or closes contrast around mid grey.",
        "fx_desc_color_colorama": "Remaps color: each pixel's brightness becomes a position on a rotating rainbow.",
        "fx_desc_color_curves": "The tone curve: fine control of light and of each color channel.",
        "fx_desc_color_exposure": "Brightens or darkens like camera exposure: multiplies light without blowing out color.",
        "fx_desc_color_invert": "The negative: every color becomes its opposite, like a badly developed film.",
        "fx_desc_color_levels": "Sets where black starts, where white ends and where the middle sits.",
        "fx_desc_color_matrix": "Mixes the R, G and B channels together: swaps, adds and crosses colors.",
        "fx_desc_color_saturation": "Makes color more vivid, or takes everything to black and white.",
        "fx_desc_color_tint": "Paints the shadows one color and the highlights another — cinema duotone.",
        "fx_desc_control_angle": "An angle you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_checkbox": "An on/off switch you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_color": "A color you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_point": "An X/Y point you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_control_slider": "A value from 0 to 100 you wire into another parameter's expression.",
        "fx_desc_distort_ripple_dissolve": "The image vanishes in circles growing from the center with a rippling edge. Animate the progress to turn it into a transition.",
        "fx_desc_distort_shake": "Deterministic shake: the layer shakes the same way every time you reopen the project, with separate frequency and axes.",
        "fx_desc_distort_turbulence": "A noise field pushes every pixel. The field evolves over time — smoke, heat, water.",
        "fx_desc_distort_warp": "Lens: push, pull, twist, sphere and corner, each with its own radius and point.",
        "fx_desc_distort_wave_warp": "A wave crosses the image — horizontal, vertical or diagonal — and can be pinned at the edges.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_cross": "Two bars, one vertical and one horizontal, scan the image reading from the wrong place. Animate the progress to turn it into a transition.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_glitchify": "Digital glitch: the image breaks into sliding blocks, the channels split apart and whole blocks jump out of place.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_signal": "Broadcast signal: lost bands, slipping sync and constant drift.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_uni_vhs": "Stylised VHS: heavy RGB split, wobble, dirty glow and vignette — the vocabulary of tape at the service of the look.",
        "fx_desc_glitch_vhs": "Real VHS: blur, smeared chroma, tracking instability, tape dropouts, scanlines and color degradation.",
        "fx_desc_key_chroma": "Removes the green or blue background and cleans the color spill on the edge.",
        "fx_desc_key_luma": "Removes the black (or the white) from the layer and lets the rest show through.",
        "fx_desc_light_deep_glow": "Glow in two halos, one tight and one wide, each with its own color: the core blows out and the surroundings fill in.",
        "fx_desc_light_glow": "Spreads the light from the bright parts: the glow that comes off the screen.",
        "fx_desc_light_rays": "Light rays coming from a point: the brightness of the highlights spreads in straight lines.",
        "fx_desc_light_sweep": "A blade of light crosses the image. With relief, it lights only where the surface faces it.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_film_damage": "Damaged film: dust, scratches, flicker, gate weave, burns and splices — each with its own control.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_grain": "Film grain: crystal at whatever size you want, luma and chroma apart, stronger in the shadows.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_halftone": "Halftone: the image becomes dots, with the grid rotated per channel so the three screens do not fight.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_holomatrix": "Hologram: the image becomes a projection, with a technical grid, scanlines and interference.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_jpeg_damage": "JPEG damage: the blocks, the ringing on edges and color at half resolution. Quality scales all three.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_minimax": "Dilates or erodes what is bright: thickens or thins a cutout and cleans up a one-pixel edge.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_motion_tile": "Repeats the image in a mosaic until it covers the frame, with optional mirror and phase.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_pixel_sort": "Sorts the pixels of each row by brightness: the image melts into streaks.",
        "fx_desc_stylize_scanlines": "Screen scanlines: the line darkens whatever is behind it, with its own height, softness and channel.",
        "fx_desc_time_echo": "Leaves a trail: copies of the image itself delayed in time, with fade.",
        "fx_desc_time_posterize": "Locks the frame rate: the image starts moving in steps, like hand-drawn animation.",
        "fx_desc_time_warp_rgb": "Each color channel comes from a different instant: red from the frame behind, blue from the frame ahead.",
        "fx_desc_transform": "Moves, rotates, scales and changes the layer's opacity without losing quality.",
